{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And you shall say: A paschal sacrifice.</b> We find פסוח and המליט (Isaiah 31:5), and the meaning is like sparing, and because HaShem spared the firstborn of Israel on account of the blood of the lamb, the lamb is called pesaḥ, as in ושחטו הפסח (Exodus 12:21). The Gaon [Saadia] said that it is from the root פסח, for the pesaḥ leans on its intact leg, and so did the destroyer do: he destroyed the firstborn of the house of the Egyptians, and pasach over the house of his Hebrew neighbor and did not destroy it; and similarly: עד מתי אתם פוסחים (1 Kings 18:21)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:33:46.770515854Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}